From 0dc81235f44149cd36068f751aa322342aa6dfc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Bradeen <mbradeen@sangoma.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:07:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] chan_pjsip: Prevent CHANNEL() deadlock during call pickup

CHANNEL() reads could previously wait on a PJSIP serializer while
holding the channel lock, resulting in a deadlock with concurrent
masquerade and update processing.

To avoid this, we now read immutable values directly and cache mutable
values via snapshot in a channel-owned datastore protected by the
channel lock. The cache is Refreshed from the session serializer so
readers no longer wait on it.

This also requires protecting T.38 state updates and termination-time
media-state swaps with the channel lock.

Fixes: #2036

Origin: upstream, https://github.com/asterisk/asterisk/pull/2193
(22 branch backport 0dc81235f44149cd36068f751aa322342aa6dfc5)
